---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import MotionStage from '@/components/motion/MotionStage.astro';
import MotionUsage from '@/components/motion/MotionUsage.astro';
import MotionTokens from '@/components/motion/MotionTokens.astro';
import Presets from '@/components/motion/scenes/Presets.astro';
import { PresetsControls } from '@/components/motion/scenes/PresetsControls';
import { chipClass } from '@/components/motionDemo';

const verbs = [
  ['appear', 'Enters through its keyframes, and leaves backward.', 'A presence: it is inserted or shown, and its exit plays when it is hidden. See Show and hide.'],
  ['disappear', 'The reverse of appear: the exit of a presence.', 'See Show and hide.'],
  ['emphasize', 'Plays its keyframes forward on each replay.', 'Replays on each change of data-state, or with play(). See Draw attention.'],
  ['layout', 'Moves the element to its new place and size when the layout around it changes.', 'Keyframes are not used: see Move to a new place.'],
  ['reveal', 'Plays when the element scrolls into view.', 'See Reveal on scroll.'],
  ['scrub', 'Follows the scroll position.', 'See Link to the scroll.'],
  ['loop', 'Plays forever, and can be paused.', 'See Loop, and pause it.'],
];
const presets = [
  ['fade', 'appear', 'Fades in.'],
  ['slide', 'appear', 'Fades in while rising 24 px.'],
  ['cascade', 'appear', 'A list entering together: each item fades in while rising 24 px, one step after the previous one (stagger normal).'],
  ['scale', 'appear', 'Fades in while growing from 80 %.'],
  ['draw', 'appear', 'Draws a path or a basic shape from nothing to its whole stroke (see SVG).'],
  ['press', 'emphasize', 'Dips to 96 % and returns.'],
  ['shake', 'emphasize', 'Shakes sideways by 6 px, then settles, to signal a refused action.'],
  ['reflow', 'layout', 'Moves to the new place and size of the element when the layout changes.'],
  ['rise', 'reveal', 'Fades in while rising 24 px, when it enters the view (stagger normal).'],
  ['parallax', 'scrub', 'Drifts from 48 px below its place to 48 px above it, across the viewport.'],
  ['rotate', 'loop', 'Turns a full turn in one second. The user can pause it.'],
  ['breathe', 'loop', 'Swells to 104 % and back in one second. The user can pause it.'],
  ['blink', 'loop', 'One dim flash each second. The user can pause it.'],
];
---
<MotionPage
  slug="presets"
  title="Motion: presets and verbs"
  description="The verbs of @udixio/motion, the defineMotion function, and the presets that are defined by importing the presets entry."
>
  <MotionStage scene="presets" label="Live example: Presets and verbs" height={[856, 2096]}>
    <Fragment slot="controls"><PresetsControls client:visible /></Fragment>
    <Presets />
    <Fragment slot="readout"><span class={`${chipClass} tracking-normal`} data-presets-readout>Press a preset to replay it.</span></Fragment>
  </MotionStage>

  <h2>How to use it</h2>
  <p>
    A motion is a named, validated description of how an element enters, leaves or emphasizes. A preset is a motion that is
    already defined: name it in <code>data-motion</code> and it plays. Your own motions are defined once with
    <code>defineMotion(name, spec)</code>; the name is kebab-case, and reserved names are refused. Identical definitions return
    the existing one; a different spec with the same name throws.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`import { defineMotion } from '@udixio/motion';

defineMotion('card-enter', {
  verb: 'appear',
  keyframes: [
    { opacity: 0, y: 24 },
    { opacity: 1, y: 0 },
  ],
  timing: 'spring.default.spatial', // optional
});`}</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li><code>verb</code> is one of the seven verbs below.</li>
    <li><code>keyframes</code> are the visual states, from the first to the last. Their fields are <code>opacity</code>, <code>x</code>, <code>y</code>, <code>scale</code>, <code>scaleX</code>, <code>scaleY</code> and <code>rotate</code>; <code>scale</code> scales both axes, and a <code>scale</code> in the same frame wins over <code>scaleX</code> and <code>scaleY</code>. <code>draw</code> and <code>along</code> are for shapes and paths (see SVG). A layout motion has no keyframes.</li>
    <li><code>timing</code> is optional: a spring token such as <code>spring.fast.spatial</code>, or <code>&#123; duration: 'duration.medium2', easing: 'easing.standard' &#125;</code>. It applies to every field.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The seven verbs</h2>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Verb</th><th>What it does</th><th>Where it is documented</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {verbs.map(([verb, does, where]) => <tr><td><code>{verb}</code></td><td>{does}</td><td>{where}</td></tr>)}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>The presets</h2>
  <p>Importing the presets entry defines these motions, usable directly in <code>data-motion</code>:</p>
  <pre><code>{`import '@udixio/motion/presets';
// or name the ones you use, as references:
import { fade, slide, reflow } from '@udixio/motion/presets';`}</code></pre>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Preset</th><th>Verb</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {presets.map(([name, verb, effect]) => <tr><td><code>{name}</code></td><td><code>{verb}</code></td><td>{effect}</td></tr>)}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    The values of the presets are provisional and are not calibrated yet. <code>cascade</code> and <code>rise</code> stagger the
    elements that enter together: see <a href="/motion/lists">Make a list appear</a> and <a href="/motion/reveal">Reveal on scroll</a>.
    <code>parallax</code> is the subject of <a href="/motion/scrub">Link to the scroll</a>, and the loops are on
    <a href="/motion/loop">Loop, and pause it</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Use it in the frameworks</h2>
  <p>
    The four frameworks name a preset in the same way: the name is the motion. The example defines nothing, and shows a
    presence, an emphasis and the replay of each.
  </p>
  <MotionUsage name="motion-presets" live={false} />

  <h2>Timing and tokens</h2>
  <p>The fade and slide presets move on the default springs. The rotate preset turns over the extra long linear curve, and the Pause loops control holds it.</p>
  <MotionTokens tokens={['spring.default.spatial', 'duration.extraLong4', 'easing.linear']} />

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <p>A preset follows the reduced-motion policy of its verb: an entry or an exit becomes a short fade, an emphasis applies its end frame, a reveal shows at once, a scrub stays still and a loop does not play. See <a href="/motion/accessibility">Reduced motion</a>.</p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Defining a name twice with different specs throws; a page that needs a variant defines a new name.</li>
    <li>The validator runs in development only; a production build trusts the definition.</li>
  </ul>
</MotionPage>
